# No corpus test artifacts on managed Postgres

Synthetic pytest/e2e documents must **never** remain on DigitalOcean Managed Postgres
(staging or production corpus). Incidents: leftover `*.example.com` / `fixture://` rows
polluted the live corpus (HF-prod-corpus-test-artifacts, 2026-09-03).

[Corpus: corpus-db-safety] [Corpus: no-live-prod-corpus-push]

## Test-artifact URL patterns (delete / refuse)

| Pattern | Examples |
|---------|----------|
| `*.example.com` | `https://batch-upsert-….example.com/`, `https://test.example.com/uj017-…` |
| `fixture://` | `fixture://corpus/en/community-resources.md` |
| localhost | `http://localhost:…`, `http://127.0.0.1:…` |

Classifier: `tests/helpers/corpus_test_artifacts.py`  
Cleanup: `uv run python scripts/ops/cleanup_corpus_test_artifacts.py --database-url "$URL"`  
Apply (managed hosts): set `VECINITA_ALLOW_CORPUS_RESET=1` and
`VECINITA_CORPUS_RESET_ACK=staging-wipe-confirmed`, then pass `--apply`.

## Do

- Run pytest / e2e against **local** Postgres only (`localhost` / `127.0.0.1` / `postgres`).
- Tear down fixture documents in the same test (or session-scoped cleanup).
- After any accidental insert into a managed DB: dry-run the cleanup script, then `--apply`
  with the corpus-reset override (AskQuestion for live prod).
- Prefer fixture hosts under `example.com` so the classifier can find leftovers.

## Do not

- Point `DATABASE_URL` at `*.ondigitalocean.com` for `pytest` / `make test-py`.
- Leave `example.com` / `fixture://` documents on staging or production after a probe.
- Use `TRUNCATE` / full corpus wipe to remove test rows — delete by URL pattern only.
- Skip AskQuestion for **live production** corpus deletes
  ([no-live-prod-corpus-push.mdc](no-live-prod-corpus-push.mdc)).

## CI

`scripts/check_corpus_test_artifacts_guard.sh` (via `make ci-guards`) asserts the
classifier, cleanup script, and this rule stay wired.
